            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0679" n="579" xml:id="pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/463: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-01T12:00:00+02:00">April 1,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 1—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. <hi rendition="#italic">Maiotis</hi> with Insull still in port. All now
                    depends on the rapidity with which the court acts and its acceptance of our
                    indictment as adequate. The Greek Government has protested against the detention
                    of the ship. The Turkish Government has replied that ship is free and remains
                    voluntarily.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
